  "notes": "USAGE:\nRefers specifically to dry roasting (no oil). The kanji {煎|い}る is often used, though ⟦{炒|い}る→炒る：13402_iru⟧ (stir-fry, which does use oil) is a related but distinct word. {煎|い}り{豆|まめ} (roasted beans) are traditionally eaten during Setsubun.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{胡麻|ごま}→胡麻：10337_goma⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{煎|い}る (to toast sesame seeds)\n- {煎|い}り{豆|まめ} (roasted beans)\n- {煎|い}りたて (freshly roasted)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{炒|いた}める→炒める：01879_itameru⟧: to stir-fry — uses oil, different cooking method\n- {焙|ほう}じる: to roast (tea) — specifically for tea leaves",
